---
import Shell from "../../../../src/astro/v2/Shell.astro";
import { lessonFixture } from "../../lib/v2-learn.mjs";
const { playgroundUrl = "#" } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="learn-section" id="lesson" aria-labelledby="learn-lesson-title">
  <header class="learn-section-heading"><div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Lesson reader</p><h2 id="learn-lesson-title">Calm prose around an exact runnable example.</h2></div><p>Reading remains primary. Run updates the result without focusing the editor; Edit is the explicit action that unlocks and focuses source on touch devices.</p></header>
  <Shell embedded={true} sidebar={true} aside={true} density="comfortable" mainId="learn-lesson-document" class="learn-lesson-shell">
    <nav slot="sidebar" class="learn-lesson-outline" aria-label="Lesson outline"><header><span>{lessonFixture.contentType}@{lessonFixture.schemaVersion}</span><strong>Outline</strong></header>{lessonFixture.sections.map((section, index) => <a href={`#lesson-${section.id}`} aria-current={index === 0 ? "page" : undefined}><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>{section.label}<small>{section.kind}</small></a>)}<a href="#lesson-states"><span>05</span>Degraded states<small>stale · unavailable</small></a></nav>
    <article class="learn-lesson-document">
      <header class="learn-lesson-header"><div><p class="learn-mono">{lessonFixture.id} · {lessonFixture.exactRevision}</p><h3>{lessonFixture.title}</h3><p>{lessonFixture.summary}</p></div><div><span class="learn-state" data-tone="signal">Current lesson</span><button type="button">Reading mode</button><button type="button">Large text</button></div></header>
      <section class="learn-objective-panel"><div><span>Learning objectives</span><ol>{lessonFixture.objectives.map((objective) => <li>{objective}</li>)}</ol></div><div><span>Prerequisites</span><div>{lessonFixture.prerequisites.map((prerequisite) => <code>{prerequisite}</code>)}</div></div></section>
      <section class="learn-reading-section" id="lesson-idea"><p class="hara-v2-kicker">01 · The idea</p><h4>A namespace is a durable name boundary.</h4><p>Source files are useful containers, but they are not the identity of a value. A namespace gives public vars a stable qualified name while the runtime records which exact source revision created the current state.</p><aside><strong>Explanation, not a compatibility rule.</strong> Products may display short aliases, but receipts, diagnostics, and cross-package references retain qualified identity when ambiguity matters.</aside></section>
      <section class="learn-live-example" id="lesson-run" data-live-example>
        <header><div><span>Runnable example</span><strong>docs.live-example + learn.lesson</strong></div><span class="learn-state" data-tone="success" data-lesson-status>Ready</span></header>
        <div class="learn-live-toolbar"><button type="button" class="learn-primary-button" data-lesson-run>Run</button><button type="button" data-lesson-edit>Edit</button><button type="button" data-lesson-reset>Reset</button><a href={playgroundUrl}>Open exact Playground</a><span>Run never focuses source</span></div>
        <div class="learn-live-grid"><label class="learn-source-editor"><span>Source · {lessonFixture.runtime.sourceRevision}</span><textarea rows="12" readonly data-lesson-editor spellcheck="false">{lessonFixture.source}</textarea></label><section class="learn-live-result" aria-live="polite"><header><span>Result</span><strong class="learn-mono" data-lesson-sequence>event {lessonFixture.runtime.eventSequence}</strong></header><pre data-lesson-result><code>{lessonFixture.result}</code></pre><p data-lesson-observation>Namespace tutorial.profile loaded in generation {lessonFixture.runtime.generation}.</p></section></div>
        <dl class="learn-runtime-envelope"><div><dt>Session</dt><dd class="learn-mono">{lessonFixture.runtime.session}</dd></div><div><dt>Generation</dt><dd>{lessonFixture.runtime.generation}</dd></div><div><dt>Backend</dt><dd>{lessonFixture.runtime.backend}</dd></div><div><dt>Capabilities</dt><dd>{lessonFixture.runtime.capabilities.join(" · ")}</dd></div><div><dt>Source revision</dt><dd class="learn-mono">{lessonFixture.runtime.sourceRevision}</dd></div><div><dt>Curriculum revision</dt><dd class="learn-mono">{lessonFixture.curriculumRevision}</dd></div></dl>
      </section>
      <section class="learn-reading-section" id="lesson-inspect"><p class="hara-v2-kicker">03 · Inspect the namespace</p><h4>Runtime state and source identity are related, not identical.</h4><p>The session can retain namespace state across evaluations, while lesson completion still targets the source and curriculum revisions shown above. Restart may advance generation without rewriting source identity; replacement creates a newly fenced session.</p><div class="learn-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Source revision creates runtime namespace state and completion evidence"><span>lesson source<br/><code>9f3c2ab7</code></span><i>→</i><span>session generation<br/><code>learn-pg-7a91 · 2</code></span><i>→</i><span>observation + attempt<br/><code>event 41</code></span></div></section>
      <section class="learn-understanding" id="lesson-check"><header><span>Check understanding</span><strong>One reason, not a trick question</strong></header><p>Why should a diagnostic retain <code>tutorial.profile/greeting</code> rather than only <code>greeting</code>?</p><div role="group"><button type="button" data-understanding-choice="scope">Because the qualified name preserves the ownership scope.</button><button type="button" data-understanding-choice="speed">Because qualified names always evaluate faster.</button><button type="button" data-understanding-choice="syntax">Because unqualified symbols are invalid Hara syntax.</button></div><output data-understanding-result>Choose the explanation that preserves identity across packages and runtimes.</output></section>
      <section class="learn-degraded-states" id="lesson-states">{lessonFixture.degradedStates.map((state) => <article data-state={state.id}><span class="learn-state" data-tone={state.id === "runtime-unavailable" ? "error" : "warning"}>{state.label}</span><p>{state.summary}</p><button type="button">Inspect exact state</button></article>)}</section>
    </article>
    <aside slot="aside" class="learn-lesson-inspector"><header><span>Glossary and references</span><strong>{lessonFixture.glossary.length + lessonFixture.related.length}</strong></header><section><span>Glossary</span>{lessonFixture.glossary.map((entry) => <details><summary>{entry.term}</summary><p>{entry.definition}</p></details>)}</section><section><span>Related</span>{lessonFixture.related.map((entry) => <a href={entry.kind === "world" ? "#world-examples" : "#teaching"}><small>{entry.kind}</small><strong>{entry.label}</strong></a>)}</section><section class="learn-lesson-authority"><span>Authority</span><dl><div><dt>Author</dt><dd>{lessonFixture.author}</dd></div><div><dt>Lesson revision</dt><dd class="learn-mono">{lessonFixture.exactRevision}</dd></div><div><dt>Status</dt><dd>published</dd></div></dl></section></aside>
  </Shell>
</section>
